b > .finished > should reject directly if already processed 508ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > process stalled jobs when starting a queue 1045ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > don't process stalled jobs when starting a queue with skipStalledCheck 1009ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > moves jobs to failed 1041ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when retrying jobs > keeps stalledCounter 1033ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > moves jobs to failed with maxStalledCount > 1 3076ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when failParentOnFailure is provided as true > should move parent to failed when child is moved to failed 1034ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when continueParentOnFailure is provided as true > should start processing parent when child is moved to failed 1033ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when ignoreDependencyOnFailure is provided as true > should move parent to waiting when child is moved to failed and save child failedReason 1033ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when removeDependencyOnFailure is provided as true > should move parent to waiting when child is moved to failed 1032ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when removeOnFail is provided as a number > keeps the specified number of jobs in failed 1031ms\n ✓ tests/stalled_jobs.test.ts > stalled jobs > when stalled jobs stall more than allowable stalled limit > when removeO