{"type":"text","timestamp":1789793153176,"sessionID":"ses_f48092514ffeIZb8Fwe8NLemBP","part":{"id":"prt_0b7fc1674001MkL6EgeftynXmq","messageID":"msg_0b7fc1087001pHE2h9Aj4ao7Di","sessionID":"ses_f48092514ffeIZb8Fwe8NLemBP","type":"text","text":"Fixed the worker ownership regression in four Lua source files.\n\n- **Completion, failure, and retries:** `removeLock.lua` now verifies the owner token before deleting a lock or allowing job mutations. Stale workers receive the existing lock-mismatch error.\n- **Lock renewal:** single-job and batch renewal now compare tokens before changing the lock, its TTL, or stalled-set membership.\n- **Immediate retry:** delayed-job promotion now runs after ownership validation, preventing rejected retries from changing queued jobs or emitting events.\n- Preserved missing-lock errors and the existing `\"0\"` token behavior for administrative operations.\n\nAdded `tests/worker_ownership.redis.test.ts` with five regression tests covering recovered jobs, stale state transitions, both renewal paths, and successful renewal/completion by the replacement owner.\n\n**Verification on Node v24.21.0**\n- `npm run build` — passed.\n- Supplied seven-file regression command — **268 tests passed**.\n- New ownership regression suite — **5 tests passed**.\n- `git diff --check` and new-test formatting check — passed.","time":{"start":1789793146484,"end":1789793153174},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_02eecc5a417b4a6b016aae137a762087d1b80f1b5f8c737328","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
